ophy. The bestrophin 4 gene is predominantly expressed in the colon. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q8NFU0","text":"Ligand-gated anion channel that allows the movement of anions across cell membranes when activated by Calcium (Ca2+) (PubMed:12907679, PubMed:18400985). Mediates the movement of hydrogencarbonate and chloride (PubMed:12907679, PubMed:18400985)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}